\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. BE Thou my vision, O Lord of my heart;
\par Naught be all else to me, save that Thou art-
\par Thou my best thought, by day or by night,
\par Walking or sleeping, Thy presence my light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Be Thou my Wisdom, Thou my true Word;
\par I ever with Thee, Thou with me, Lord;
\par Thou my great Father, I Thy true son;
\par Thou in me dwelling, and I with Thee one.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Be Thou my battle-shield, sword for the fight,
\par Be Thou my dignity, Thou my delight.
\par Thou my soul's shelter, Thou my high tower:
\par Raise Thou me heavenward, O Power of my power.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Riches I heed not, nor man's empty praise,
\par Thou mine inheritance, now and always:
\par Thou and Thou only, first in my heart,
\par High King of heaven, my treasure Thou art.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. High King of heaven, after victory won,
\par May I reach heaven's joys, O bright heaven's Sun!
\par Heart of my own heart, whatever befall,
\par Still be my Vision, O Ruler of all.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

